WitOS has no Linux system call instruction contract (plan step V2.4): compiler-rt's __clear_cache for RISC-V issues the riscv_flush_icache system call with an inline ecall, which on WitOS would reach the kernel's ABI-1 dispatch with a Linux number. The branch calls musl's __riscv_flush_icache instead, which takes the C library's system call path, where the system layer publishes the executable mappings of the range through the kernel's CODE_PUBLISH (src/Substrate/libc/memory.c); CoreCLR's PAL takes the same path through syscall(), and NativeAOT's runtime reaches it through __builtin___clear_cache. The declaration replaces the Linux header, which musl does not install.

